rf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, February to March has come in under 90% of normal in 35 of 75 years since 1951 on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids, more than any other pair. In 2026 so far, March to April sits at 54% of normal on the middle. Grid 20284 had its driest year in 2007 at 66% of normal. A preliminary estimate puts August to September 2026 at 94.1 on grid 20284, and that figure can still change.</p>"}
